<article class="env-lemma" id="033L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/033L">Lemma <span data-tag="033L">28.7.4</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an integral scheme. Then $X$ is normal if and only if for every nonempty affine open $U \subset X$ the ring $\mathcal{O}_ X(U)$ is a normal domain. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/030B" data-tag="030B">10.37.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>